<description>&lt;p&gt;Egypt reopened its embassy in Tripoli after a 12‑year closure, restoring a diplomatic presence that had been absent. ISIS militants killed a young Christian man in Libya after he refused to deny Jesus, showing continued extremist attacks on individuals. The WHO identified 111 children with malnutrition in Qatrun, warning of worsening health services. Migrant vessels departing from Libya have suffered deadly shipwrecks off Crete, with at least 20 migrants killed in recent incidents. Combat intensity remains low, with 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijwFBVV95cUxNN1RnOEJkbERKWVhHcXc2NkV6c3RSWS1aVHk1SFhRZExUU3VkWWo3dnVXOFFsNDZxUWRYS2tha3M5Njl0QUVKNGktR3NITURSazV6bzVBazJvWDhDbGFzNHVWRnhjWlprclhoVnJzOXFWVjRyYTY4dU40dHBaZGpEako1NmtqLXBWY3BaV0hhaw?oc=5&quot;&gt;www.christiandaily.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxQRkdEWnJyMlRPQkNYamR3SmpCSWxvSkNsNGM4anlaXzB4MTEzc0dwbldVVzZrMU5YZHhrcF9RaUFEWnl3djlqSmJ1ZUI3M3ZIOUtqTVhmTWdqNFp5enFnMXBjbFNkUkgxMDBZeHF0U2VjZWxQWGxmRnV6aWFiODZDSzNGUDZJaDlpNFN1QUpWRzFUSTE4amtZcFBKMk_SAZsBQVVfeXFMT1ZwQ3pVUm41SEprdXQ5QUt3ZDJaNEQ1aTdUbGlHZlhXbkRvRG11akdwSFhUNDR2OWozM0lfbGU2TXZSQVhPcVozUGp3WTYtUlBSV255MmpYNndSN3AzQXVvS0lnc0w3d1pSeXVkR2NfeFNzdzdqY0ZSQk5KUUJWejk0eDBZWEZJSWVoakdNNm1rLUhGNVFya3hLTG8?oc=5&quot;&gt;Modern Ghana&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxQZkJ4MnRIOVFTNFpGTlVoWXhqRUFRbVBiNmlHN2czWE5tV19ZQW13ZUlRTDRSY2tFcG83WDVoY0lJVDZ3RkpuaHpSeVR0MndXLS1xaF8tOEROQlJYT0tKbjlZUHJiWDgyRXpRdml6UTNnV0ZGb3VjdG5ZRFVqSUU5ZzdBMXRZTHVCYUdkU1B1Z3hqQnVtZGpibEZnSHhKdjl2a0NoemFQRGhRYkc1YU5Lal9TNXRHYWc?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Libya Observer&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;h